      "Historic Fes... The ancient city is vibrant with brilliant colors, architecture, and traditional crafts. As Morocco's oldest imperial city, its walls are adorned with breathtaking mosaics and intricate geometric designs that have stood the test of time, telling the story of successive Moroccan dynasties and unleashing the imagination of all who wander through. This city, founded by the Idrissid dynasty, is home not only to many palaces but also to the world's oldest university, the University of Al-Qarawiyyin. Wandering its alleyways allows you to delight in the finest architectural details and traditional handicrafts, and provides an opportunity to delve into a city of deep scholarly and spiritual character.",
